WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.931
Are your emails landing in spam?
Your DNS records could be the reason.

00:00:05.531 --> 00:00:10.501
Click the checker in your toolbar, type your
domain or an email address, and press Check.

00:00:10.851 --> 00:00:14.121
In seconds, each record gets
Pass, Check or Fix,

00:00:14.121 --> 00:00:16.334
so you know exactly what needs work.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.449
Here's what good looks like.

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:24.885
SPF: one record, ending in ~all or -all,
with ten DNS lookups or fewer.

00:00:25.335 --> 00:00:29.047
DKIM: a key is found, ideally 2048 bits.

00:00:29.247 --> 00:00:31.167
Custom selector? Add it here.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:37.121
DMARC: set to quarantine or reject,
with a reporting address for daily reports.

00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:40.878
And MX should point to
your email provider's mail servers.

00:00:41.478 --> 00:00:45.062
Anything off comes with a plain-English fix
and a free guide.

00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:48.683
Copy report copies it all
for whoever runs your DNS.

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:51.907
It's free, with no sign-up
and no permissions.

00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:56.647
SPF, DKIM and DMARC Checker, by imisofts.
